+# Authored Markdown → knowledge bundle
+
+## Goal
+Turn authored Markdown documents into a `KnowledgeBundle` (`knowledge-bundle/v1`) so the
+existing bundle import can load authored content. Output is deterministic: the same
+content always yields the same `bundle_digest`.
+
+## Scope
+Included: a new pure domain module `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` (Markdown
+splitting, slugs, section keys, section choices, bundle building).
+Unchanged: `bundle.py`, `models.py`, import/application/infrastructure code, DB schema,
+and the on-disk bundle format. No IO in the new module.
+
+## Interfaces
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class Section: heading: str; path: tuple[str, ...]; ordinal: int; blocks: list[BlockRecord]
+@dataclass(frozen=True) class AuthoredDocument: key: str; title: str; markdown: str
+    kind: DocumentKind = DocumentKind.GENERAL_MONOGRAPH; source_title: str | None = None  # defaults to title
+
+def split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[Section]
+def slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str
+def section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str
+def bundle_document_key(collection_key: str, document_key: str) -> str   # "<collection>:<document>"
+def section_choices(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument]) -> list[tuple[str, str]]
+def build_bundle(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument],
+                 glossary: Sequence[GlossaryEntry],
+                 colloquial: Sequence[ColloquialMappingRecord]) -> KnowledgeBundle
+```
+
+## Approach
+- `split_markdown`: single pass over lines tracking fenced-code state (``` / ~~~, closing
+  fence same char and at least as long). ATX headings (`#`..`######`) outside fences open
+  a section; a heading stack gives `path` (enclosing headings including the section's own
+  heading; `heading` is the last). Text before the first heading (or all of a
+  headingless document) is a section titled `fallback_heading` with empty path. Sections
+  with no non-blank content are dropped; `ordinal` counts the kept sections from 0.
+- Blocks: outside fences, a run of lines starting with `|` is one TABLE block with
+  `table_key` `t1`, `t2`, … numbered across the document; the text between is a stripped
+  PROSE block (blank-only text yields none). Fenced code stays in prose.
+- `slugify`: NFD-decompose, map `đ`→`d`, drop combining marks and non-ASCII, lowercase,
+  words `[a-z0-9]+` joined by `-`, truncated to `max_length` without a trailing hyphen.
+- `section_key`: `<doc>#<slug parts joined "/">`, empty path → `<doc>#body`.
+- Bundle document key = `collection.key:document.key`. Documents sorted by key. Section
+  keys within a document must be unique (the import rejects duplicates), so a repeated
+  key gets `-2`, `-3`, … appended; `section_choices` and `build_bundle` share one helper
+  so keys agree. Choices follow the bundle's order (documents by key, sections by
+  ordinal); label = title + path joined with ` › ` (title alone for empty path).
+- `build_bundle`: one `SectionRecord` per section (`context_path=list(path)`), glossary
+  as given, colloquial mappings with unknown section keys removed from `section_keys`
+  (the mapping itself stays). Manifest: collection key/title, document/section counts,
+  fixed generator (`pharma-agent-authoring`, version `1`, build id `authoring`), empty
+  `source_digests`/`files` — no timestamps or randomness.
+
+## Testing
+`tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`: splitting (fences, fallback, empty sections,
+paths, tables numbering, prose stripping), slugify (Vietnamese, max length), keys,
+choices, bundle shape, unknown colloquial keys removed, determinism (same digest, input
+order independent), duplicate headings, and that `write_bundle` accepts the result.
